# Target C-II — common-outer collapsed blocks pay anchor-length variation

**Date:** 2026-09-18  
**Status:** proved candidate; scoped source-separation reduction, theorem-state authority unchanged  
**Scope:** collapsed support-six block whose six outside trains terminate at one common outer host  
**Certificate:** `research/verify_target_c_support6_collapsed_outer_length_variation_2026_09_18.py`

Assume the six one-anchor trains of a collapsed support-six block all terminate at the
same outer face `O`, remain pairwise noncrossing, and meet the outer sector in six
distinct consecutive train corridors. Let `ell_i` be the positive integer number of
unit contact-edge occurrences in the `i`th train, in cyclic outer order. The collapsed
dual mode gives a `3+3` sign word `s_i in {+1,-1}` for the six anchor directions.

At two consecutive outer corridors with opposite signs, the two adjacent dual source
regions are separated by the signed train displacement

\[
(\ell_i-\ell_{i+1})e_1.
\]

If the lengths were equal, those two distinct source regions would have the same
source point, or the two corridors would induce duplicate contact edges. Both are
excluded by the simple, unit-separated source hypothesis. Consequently

\[
s_i\ne s_{i+1}\quad\Longrightarrow\quad \ell_i\ne\ell_{i+1}.
\tag{OV.1}
\]

Every cyclic `3+3` sign word has at least two sign transitions. Since the `ell_i` are
integers, (OV.1) implies the exact finite payment

\[
\boxed{\sum_{i=1}^6|\ell_i-\ell_{i+1}|\ge2.}
\tag{OV.2}
\]

The all-outer minimum-crossing enumeration sharpens the finite alternatives.  Of the
48 six-crossing boundary orders, 36 have two sign transitions and 12 have six sign
transitions for the fixed collapsed `+++---` label word.  In general, if `T(s)` is
the number of cyclic sign transitions, the same argument gives

\[
\boxed{\sum_i|\ell_i-\ell_{i+1}|\ge T(s).}
\tag{OV.3}
\]

Thus the six-transition subfamily pays at least six units of integer anchor-length
variation.  The crossing graph in every six-crossing minimum pattern is also exactly
one `C_6` on six internal trains plus six isolated internal trains; triangle-freeness
is therefore not the only available finite structure, although it is still not by
itself a contradiction.

The certificate exhausts all labelled `3+3` sign words and small positive integer
length vectors; the combinatorial proof itself is the two-transition argument.

## Dependency chain

```text
collapsed support-six dual mode
  -> three plus / three minus parallel anchor directions
  -> common-outer cyclic order
  -> opposite-sign transitions have unequal integer train lengths
  -> total anchor-length variation >= 2
```

This is not a global exclusion. The current collapsed branch allows anchor trains to
attach to several activated faces, and the simple outer-sector hypothesis is not yet a
canonical theorem. The result identifies a concrete source-level currency to couple to
the train-length/outer-walk ledger when the common-outer branch is isolated.

**Disposition:** proved candidate at scoped reduction; positive-slack collapsed branch
and C-II remain open.
